      "action": "opening_fact_true",
      "detail": "Aspose.Words FOSS for Python reads `.md`, `.txt`, .docx, and .doc files and writes `.md`, `.pdf`, and `.txt` files. It converts documents between these formats using its `Document` class and associated writers and readers. The package provides a `light_document_model` for memory-efficient processing and supports reading Markdown with `MarkdownLoadOptions`. It is implemented in Python and distributed under the MIT license.",
